---A CoordGrid represents a position within the game world's tile system, in Grid units, as opposed to the 3D world
---position found in CoordFine, which is in Fine units.
---@class CoordGrid
---@field level integer (Writeable) The level of this CoordGrid. Valid range is 0-3.
---@field x integer (Writeable) The world tile X of this CoordGrid, in Grid units. Valid range is 0-12799.
---@field z integer (Writeable) The world tile Z of this CoordGrid, in Grid units. Valid range is 0-12799.
---@field mapSquareX integer (Read-only) The mapsquare X of this CoordGrid, in Grid units. Valid range is 0-199.
---@field mapSquareZ integer (Read-only) The mapsquare Z of this CoordGrid, in Grid units. Valid range is 0-199.
---@field localX integer (Read-only) The local tile X of this CoordGrid, in Grid units. Valid range is 0-63.
---@field localZ integer (Read-only) The local tile Z of this CoordGrid, in Grid units. Valid range is 0-63.
---@field valid boolean (Read-only) Whether this coordinate is valid.
CoordGrid = {}

---Constructs a CoordGrid from the provided numeric value.
---
---This value is a packed representation of the coordinate, useful for storing as a single 32-bit integer. The
---coordinate data is packed as follows: `(level << 28) | (x << 14) | (z)`
---
---Also see CoordGrid:ToPacked
---@param bitPacked integer The packed representation of a CoordGrid.
---@return CoordGrid
---@overload fun(level: integer, mapSquareX: integer, mapSquareZ: integer): CoordGrid
---@overload fun(level: integer, mapSquareX: integer, mapSquareZ: integer, localTileX: integer, localTileZ: integer): CoordGrid
---@overload fun(level: integer, position: Vector3): CoordGrid
---@overload fun(coordFine: CoordFine): CoordGrid
---@overload fun(coordGrid: CoordGrid): CoordGrid
function CoordGrid.new(bitPacked) end

---Returns a CoordGrid constructed from the provided CoordFine.
---
---The value of `coordFine.level` is copied directly. The values of `coordFine.position.x` and `coordFine.position.z`
---are converted to Grid Units. The value of `coordFine.position.y` is discarded. The Fine->Grid unit conversion is as
---follows:
---
---Also see CoordFine:ToCoordGrid and CoordGrid(coordFine)
---@param coordFine CoordFine A CoordFine position.
---@return CoordGrid # A CoordGrid position.
function CoordGrid.FromCoordFine(coordFine) end

---Returns a numeric value which is a packed representation of the coordinate, useful for storing as a single 32-bit
---integer. The coordinate data is packed as follows: `(level << 28) | (x << 14) | (z)`
---@return integer # The numeric value representing a CoordGrid.
function CoordGrid:ToPacked() end

